&lt;h2 id="location-description"&gt;Location Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An ancient city of Campania destroyed by the volcanic eruption of Mt. Vesuvius in CE 79, Pompeii was named as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1997.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="sublocation"&gt;Sublocation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2 id="insula"&gt;Insula&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/place/italia/regio_i_latium_et_campania/pompeii/region_ii/insula_vii/"&gt;Insula VII&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="keywords"&gt;Keywords&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/search/?q=porticoes"&gt;porticoes&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a class="id" target="_blank" href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300004145" title="Art and Architecture Thesaurus (Getty)"&gt;AAT:300004145&lt;/a&gt;)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/search/?q=palaestrae"&gt;palaestrae&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a class="id" target="_blank" href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300007301" title="Art and Architecture Thesaurus (Getty)"&gt;AAT:300007301&lt;/a&gt;)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Colonnaded &lt;a href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300004145" target="_blank"&gt;porticoes&lt;/a&gt; encircled the &lt;a href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300007301" target="_blank"&gt;palaestra&lt;/a&gt; on the south, west and north. A large swimming pool (34.55 m x 22.25 m) was located in the center. Casts made of tree cavities planted eight meters apart in two rows around the north, west and south sides of the enclosed area indicated that these were plane trees, just under one hundred years old.&lt;/p&gt;
